1
00:00:00,980 --> 00:00:02,980
Previously on Captain Tsubasa.

2
00:00:03,730 --> 00:00:06,980
Ozora Tsubasa, who loves football dearly...

3
00:00:06,980 --> 00:00:11,280
...happens upon a dispute over a football field in his new town.

4
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:14,700
It is between Wakabayashi Genzo and Ishizaki Ryo.

5
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:18,950
With his brimming confidence, Wakabayashi, who has never conceded a goal...

6
00:00:18,950 --> 00:00:23,370
...nullifies all the attempts of the students Ishizaki gathered.

7
00:00:24,330 --> 00:00:27,090
The performance Wakabayashi displayed...

8
00:00:27,090 --> 00:00:28,920
...captivates Tsubasa's interest...

9
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:31,840
...and he challenges him!

10
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:34,260
Wakabayashi, glad you came!

11
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:37,930
This is the one who challenged you!

12
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:39,760
Don't be ridiculous!

13
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:43,270
A newcomer like him can't kick that powerfully!

14
00:00:43,770 --> 00:00:47,610
Whether it's true or not, we'll see the answer right now!

15
00:00:48,150 --> 00:00:49,900
Here!

16
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:52,110
Watch out! Here it comes!

17
00:00:58,580 --> 00:01:01,450
Was it fate or coincidence?

18
00:01:01,450 --> 00:01:07,460
In any case, Ozora Tsubasa and Wakabayashi Genzo had met.

19
00:01:14,340 --> 00:01:16,260
How about that, Wakabayashi?!

20
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:18,760
You've seen his real power now!

21
00:01:20,850 --> 00:01:23,350
# Ozora Tsubasa requests a match #

22
00:01:25,850 --> 00:01:28,560
Will you accept my challenge?

23
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:32,070
Why do you challenge me?

24
00:01:32,070 --> 00:01:37,320
He saw you saving shots from the rugby and baseball players the other day.

25
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:40,490
Is that so.

26
00:01:40,490 --> 00:01:42,040
Captain!

27
00:01:42,450 --> 00:01:43,580
Was it you guys?

28
00:01:43,580 --> 00:01:44,950
What happened?

29
00:01:44,950 --> 00:01:47,370
Weren't you going to head home?

30
00:01:47,370 --> 00:01:49,130
Perfect timing.

31
00:01:50,710 --> 00:01:53,090
That kid kicks pretty hard.

32
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:57,090
But if he thinks that alone is enough to play football, he's sorely mistaken.

33
00:01:57,090 --> 00:01:58,340
What?!

34
00:01:58,340 --> 00:02:00,800
If you want to challenge me...

35
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:04,180
...you must get past all of them by yourself!

36
00:02:04,180 --> 00:02:05,100
What?!

37
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:08,350
Only then will I accept your challenge!

38
00:03:45,370 --> 00:03:47,950
Episode 2: Flying!
Translation: ARE-YOU-SURE
www.areyousuresubs.com

39
00:03:45,370 --> 00:03:47,950
Captain, what's the meaning of this?

40
00:03:47,950 --> 00:03:49,700
As I said.

41
00:03:49,700 --> 00:03:51,870
You will follow my orders.

42
00:03:51,870 --> 00:03:53,920
Alright, but...

43
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:56,040
Who's that shrimp?

44
00:03:57,340 --> 00:04:04,430
# Ozora Tsubasa requests a match #

45
00:03:57,710 --> 00:03:59,420
What's this?

46
00:03:59,420 --> 00:04:04,430
He launched this ball all the way from a very far distance to my home.

47
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:13,850
So you're going to accept this challenge, Captain?

48
00:04:13,850 --> 00:04:16,230
Yes, exactly.

49
00:04:16,650 --> 00:04:18,070
Hey, Wakabayashi!

50
00:04:18,070 --> 00:04:21,240
Tsubasa wants to challenge you!

51
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:24,200
Making him take on the entire B team all alone is absurd!

52
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:27,120
If he doesn't want to do it, he can just go home.

53
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:29,490
You're so unfair, Wakabayashi!

54
00:04:29,490 --> 00:04:31,040
I'll do it.

55
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:34,210
What?! You will? Are you serious?

56
00:04:34,210 --> 00:04:36,580
Because he's about to accept my challenge.

57
00:04:36,580 --> 00:04:40,000
But hold on! You're one against that many!

58
00:04:41,340 --> 00:04:45,180
I didn't quite catch what's going on, but it looks fun.

59
00:04:45,180 --> 00:04:47,470
He's got guts to challenge the Captain.

60
00:04:47,470 --> 00:04:50,270
He's already lost.

61
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:53,690
Don't worry. Leave it to me.

62
00:04:53,690 --> 00:04:54,560
What?

63
00:04:55,020 --> 00:04:57,480
Truly a strange kid.

64
00:05:09,780 --> 00:05:11,160
Hey, Tsubasa!

65
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:14,040
Just realized...

66
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:16,750
...can you play in those shoes?

67
00:05:19,630 --> 00:05:22,670
Yes. Right now I only have these with me.

68
00:05:22,670 --> 00:05:25,130
What? That's impossible.

69
00:05:26,970 --> 00:05:30,600
Even if they're the B team, they're pretty good.

70
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:34,310
Plus you're alone. Two disadvantages at once.

71
00:05:34,310 --> 00:05:37,150
You're like a bird with broken wings.

72
00:05:37,150 --> 00:05:38,560
But...

73
00:05:38,560 --> 00:05:42,190
Does anyone have extra cleats? Lend him some.

74
00:05:42,190 --> 00:05:43,570
O-Okay.

75
00:05:43,570 --> 00:05:45,490
Thank you, Wakabayashi-kun.

76
00:05:45,490 --> 00:05:47,110
I don't need your thanks.

77
00:05:47,110 --> 00:05:50,990
I'm only doing this so you can't blame the cleats when you lose.

78
00:05:56,460 --> 00:05:58,580
Then it's time for the challenge.

79
00:06:05,420 --> 00:06:08,930
I'm sure I've seen that man somewhere.

80
00:06:09,590 --> 00:06:11,220
I wonder if he'll manage.

81
00:06:15,850 --> 00:06:17,440
Can you see?

82
00:06:18,020 --> 00:06:20,900
The one who brought you here.

83
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:23,900
His name is Wakabayashi-kun.

84
00:06:23,900 --> 00:06:26,650
He's talking to the ball again.

85
00:06:26,650 --> 00:06:31,030
He won last year's national championship without conceding a single goal.

86
00:06:31,030 --> 00:06:33,700
So he's a magnificent goalkeeper.

87
00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:37,250
But first I have to get past the other players...

88
00:06:37,250 --> 00:06:40,170
...so I can challenge that goalkeeper.

89
00:06:40,170 --> 00:06:42,420
What's he rambling about?

90
00:06:42,420 --> 00:06:44,340
He's talking to the ball.

91
00:06:44,340 --> 00:06:46,710
He's clearly nuts.

92
00:06:47,380 --> 00:06:51,840
You saved my life when I was very little...

93
00:06:51,840 --> 00:06:53,970
...but I need your help again.

94
00:06:57,730 --> 00:07:01,480
I want to challenge him at all costs.

95
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:05,280
What are you waiting for?!

96
00:07:05,280 --> 00:07:07,240
Hurry up and get the ball!

97
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:08,780
O-Okay!

98
00:07:08,780 --> 00:07:09,950
Alright, let's go!

99
00:07:09,950 --> 00:07:10,740
Okay!

100
00:07:12,450 --> 00:07:13,870
Ready?

101
00:07:13,870 --> 00:07:14,780
Let's go.

102
00:07:14,780 --> 00:07:15,700
Come on!

103
00:07:23,460 --> 00:07:24,340
What?

104
00:07:27,010 --> 00:07:29,050
He got past three players instantly!

105
00:07:47,780 --> 00:07:49,570
What is this?

106
00:07:49,570 --> 00:07:52,280
Taking a shot from under the bus...

107
00:07:52,280 --> 00:07:54,490
These dribbles...

108
00:07:54,490 --> 00:07:57,370
Even at this young age...

109
00:07:57,370 --> 00:07:59,500
...he's already become friends with the ball!

110
00:08:00,290 --> 00:08:01,710
No doubt about it.

111
00:08:01,710 --> 00:08:03,670
This kid...

112
00:08:03,670 --> 00:08:05,340
That's the kid!

113
00:08:05,340 --> 00:08:07,590
Go, Tsubasa!

114
00:08:10,470 --> 00:08:12,220
Damn...

115
00:08:12,220 --> 00:08:15,220
Don't let him shoot! Block him!

116
00:08:21,940 --> 00:08:23,600
He's flying!

117
00:08:24,350 --> 00:08:25,360
What?!

118
00:08:34,990 --> 00:08:36,240
Go in!

119
00:08:40,750 --> 00:08:42,620
The ball is still in play!

120
00:08:45,250 --> 00:08:47,540
It might be a bit of a waste, but...

121
00:08:47,540 --> 00:08:50,260
...this contest is worth a little whiskey!

122
00:08:55,260 --> 00:08:57,640
I knew it, that man...

123
00:08:57,640 --> 00:09:00,390
...is the forward for the Brazilian national team...

124
00:09:00,390 --> 00:09:02,060
...Roberto Hongo!

125
00:09:02,060 --> 00:09:04,600
Finish the cross!

126
00:09:14,570 --> 00:09:17,820
This was how the first challenge between

127
00:09:17,820 --> 00:09:22,370
...Ozora Tsubasa and Wakabayashi Genzo came to be.

128
00:09:22,370 --> 00:09:24,660
No one could have known that this would later...

129
00:09:24,660 --> 00:09:30,960
...lead Japanese football to tremendous heights!

130
00:09:45,690 --> 00:09:47,730
That's it! Goal!

131
00:10:04,370 --> 00:10:05,040
Genzo!

132
00:10:05,040 --> 00:10:06,790
Captain!

133
00:10:06,790 --> 00:10:07,540
Get a grip.

134
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:09,130
What's wrong?

135
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:12,630
Are you okay?

136
00:10:12,630 --> 00:10:13,680
Don't touch me!

137
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:15,590
What's the matter with you, Wakabayashi?!

138
00:10:15,590 --> 00:10:17,300
Shut up!

139
00:10:26,430 --> 00:10:27,940
Hey, he's bleeding.

140
00:10:29,190 --> 00:10:31,190
Captain!

141
00:10:31,190 --> 00:10:32,690
Genzo!

142
00:10:34,150 --> 00:10:36,110
I lost.

143
00:10:36,110 --> 00:10:39,160
I lost to this shrimp.

144
00:10:41,370 --> 00:10:43,870
Ozora Tsubasa, isn't it?

145
00:10:43,870 --> 00:10:44,620
Yes.

146
00:10:45,330 --> 00:10:46,500
A match.

147
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:47,540
What?

148
00:10:47,540 --> 00:10:50,290
We'll play a match, a match!

149
00:10:51,250 --> 00:10:55,300
This challenge can't be settled like this!

150
00:10:55,300 --> 00:10:57,420
Only a match can decide it!

151
00:10:57,420 --> 00:11:00,640
I'll accept your challenge at the interschool tournament!

152
00:11:00,640 --> 00:11:01,970
Interschool?

153
00:11:02,930 --> 00:11:04,390
Wait, Wakabayashi!

154
00:11:06,810 --> 00:11:07,890
Listen!

155
00:11:07,890 --> 00:11:10,900
In the interschool tournament, if you score even one goal...

156
00:11:10,900 --> 00:11:13,650
...I'll admit defeat.

157
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:16,480
Alright, I understand.

158
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:19,280
It doesn't matter who wins the match.

159
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:22,910
We'll see if you can score a goal against me!

160
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:32,100
Translation: ARE-YOU-SURE
www.areyousuresubs.com

161
00:11:40,550 --> 00:11:42,010
Ishizaki.

162
00:11:42,010 --> 00:11:45,050
Until the interschool tournament, use this field.

163
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:47,930
Do some training...

164
00:11:47,930 --> 00:11:50,560
...so you don't get rusty.

165
00:11:51,810 --> 00:11:52,940
Let's go!

166
00:11:52,940 --> 00:11:54,060
Yes, sir!

167
00:11:54,940 --> 00:11:56,440
Hey, wait!

168
00:11:57,570 --> 00:11:59,570
The cleats, the cleats.

169
00:11:59,570 --> 00:12:01,110
R-Right...

170
00:12:01,110 --> 00:12:01,910
I don't want them!

171
00:12:06,240 --> 00:12:07,870
Thanks for the cleats.

172
00:12:07,870 --> 00:12:10,120
You're welcome.

173
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:12,920
See you at the interschool tournament!

174
00:12:21,170 --> 00:12:25,050
Wakabayashi really lost it, huh.

175
00:12:25,050 --> 00:12:28,310
I thought he was going to hit you.

176
00:12:28,310 --> 00:12:31,980
But scoring that goal was truly great.

177
00:12:31,980 --> 00:12:32,940
Thanks.

178
00:12:33,770 --> 00:12:35,360
You actually managed to get it in.

179
00:12:38,070 --> 00:12:39,480
Ishizaki-kun!

180
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:39,900
Here.

181
00:12:42,070 --> 00:12:43,450
Sorry.

182
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:48,580
I may not look it, but I'm the captain of the Nankatsu football team.

183
00:12:49,370 --> 00:12:50,830
Ishizaki-kun, pass!

184
00:12:52,830 --> 00:12:53,960
Okay!

185
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:57,920
Next time, I'll introduce you to the team.

186
00:12:57,920 --> 00:13:00,170
Okay, thanks.

187
00:13:00,170 --> 00:13:03,380
By the way, what's this interschool tournament they were talking about?

188
00:13:03,840 --> 00:13:06,180
That?

189
00:13:06,180 --> 00:13:11,020
First, remember that Nankatsu and Shutetsu are rivals!

190
00:13:11,020 --> 00:13:11,890
Rivals?

191
00:13:11,890 --> 00:13:14,520
Yes. That wretched Shutetsu!

192
00:13:15,770 --> 00:13:19,650
Their football team is very good.

193
00:13:19,650 --> 00:13:22,240
All the good players are with them...

194
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:24,280
...while we only have the lousy ones!

195
00:13:27,660 --> 00:13:32,410
Between Nankatsu and Shutetsu, there's nothing but rivalry!

196
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:35,670
Today's issue over the football field...

197
00:13:35,670 --> 00:13:38,250
...was just one of those rivalries.

198
00:13:38,250 --> 00:13:41,670
You said we could share the field, but...

199
00:13:41,670 --> 00:13:43,670
...that's not really the issue here!

200
00:13:45,840 --> 00:13:47,760
That's how it looks.

201
00:13:47,760 --> 00:13:51,010
As for the interschool tournament...

202
00:13:51,510 --> 00:13:54,270
...it's an annual contest between

203
00:13:54,270 --> 00:13:57,850
all the sports clubs of Nankatsu and Shutetsu.

204
00:13:57,850 --> 00:14:00,360
It's like a festival.

205
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:04,440
In this city, it's a bigger deal than the sports festival!

206
00:14:04,780 --> 00:14:06,650
What? That's amazing.

207
00:14:06,650 --> 00:14:12,950
All our clubs are as good as Shutetsu's. Except for football.

208
00:14:13,790 --> 00:14:19,500
That's why we're always a burden to the other clubs.

209
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:26,880
But with you on the team, we'll definitely put on a good show against Shutetsu!

210
00:14:26,880 --> 00:14:28,050
Yes.

211
00:14:32,970 --> 00:14:33,680
There!

212
00:14:34,390 --> 00:14:35,930
Ugh, I missed!

213
00:14:41,020 --> 00:14:43,270
Thanks for just now.

214
00:14:43,270 --> 00:14:46,190
What? Don't mention it.

215
00:14:46,650 --> 00:14:49,360
You made me a nice offer.

216
00:14:50,910 --> 00:14:52,780
Ozora Tsubasa-kun.

217
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:56,290
I'm Roberto Hongo.

218
00:14:56,290 --> 00:14:57,370
Nice to meet you.

219
00:14:58,990 --> 00:15:00,560
Roberto Hongo!

220
00:15:00,760 --> 00:15:04,090
I know you! I've watched your matches countless times!

221
00:15:05,210 --> 00:15:06,590
Thank you!

222
00:15:06,590 --> 00:15:08,970
I'm very glad to meet you too.

223
00:15:08,970 --> 00:15:11,720
He smells of alcohol! He's just a drunk!

224
00:15:11,720 --> 00:15:14,310
Hello. Are you Tsubasa's friend?

225
00:15:14,310 --> 00:15:15,060
Yes.

226
00:15:15,060 --> 00:15:17,810
I'm Roberto Hongo. Nice to meet you.

227
00:15:17,810 --> 00:15:18,980
Nice to meet you.

228
00:15:18,980 --> 00:15:21,650
Do you also love football?

229
00:15:21,650 --> 00:15:23,440
Yes, I do, but...

230
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:24,730
Is that so?

231
00:15:26,190 --> 00:15:28,110
I absolutely love football!

232
00:15:28,860 --> 00:15:31,240
He's clearly nuts.

233
00:15:32,160 --> 00:15:37,250
How about I coach you until the interschool tournament?

234
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:41,500
A drunk coaching our team?!

235
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:44,840
Exactly. It's not like I'm coaching the sumo club.

236
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:45,840
Hold on!

237
00:15:45,840 --> 00:15:49,510
Don't underestimate us just because we're an elementary school club!

238
00:15:49,510 --> 00:15:52,680
Just because you put in a cross doesn't make you something special!

239
00:15:52,680 --> 00:15:54,850
Anyone can do that!

240
00:15:54,850 --> 00:15:58,600
Hey, hey. That's harsh.

241
00:15:58,600 --> 00:16:01,350
What are you laughing at?! You're getting on my nerves.

242
00:16:01,350 --> 00:16:05,190
Besides, nobody wants a drunk as a coach.

243
00:16:06,230 --> 00:16:07,400
In that case...

244
00:16:07,400 --> 00:16:09,030
...let me show you.

245
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:16,580
He took the ball so easily.

246
00:16:33,300 --> 00:16:34,800
What's he doing?

247
00:16:41,980 --> 00:16:42,940
Let's go!

248
00:16:47,520 --> 00:16:49,610
What? It didn't even go in!

249
00:16:59,580 --> 00:17:01,080
What?!

250
00:17:08,550 --> 00:17:09,920
There it is.

251
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:11,300
Perfect!

252
00:17:11,300 --> 00:17:13,420
A-Amazing!

253
00:17:13,420 --> 00:17:16,470
So? Do you want me as coach?

254
00:17:16,470 --> 00:17:18,810
I do, of course I do!

255
00:17:20,600 --> 00:17:22,930
Absolutely! We're in your hands. Right, Tsubasa?

256
00:17:24,850 --> 00:17:25,690
What?

257
00:17:25,690 --> 00:17:27,190
There!

258
00:17:29,230 --> 00:17:30,190
Tsubasa!

259
00:17:34,450 --> 00:17:35,570
Could it be...

260
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:46,710
Tsubasa!

261
00:17:48,460 --> 00:17:50,500
Hey, are you okay?

262
00:17:51,460 --> 00:17:53,260
That was tough.

263
00:17:53,260 --> 00:17:56,800
But you jump pretty well, though.

264
00:17:56,800 --> 00:18:00,140
Exactly. I have high expectations for you, Tsubasa.

265
00:18:00,140 --> 00:18:01,310
Really?

266
00:18:01,310 --> 00:18:02,310
Yes.

267
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:07,480
Alright, once more.

268
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:09,810
You can't do it that quickly!

269
00:18:09,810 --> 00:18:11,690
I can!

270
00:18:11,690 --> 00:18:13,320
What?

271
00:18:15,070 --> 00:18:19,200
He just saw my move and he's already trying it.

272
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:23,240
No wonder he improves so fast.

273
00:18:27,120 --> 00:18:31,960
He's someone who's determined to replicate any technique he sees.

274
00:18:32,840 --> 00:18:34,010
What?

275
00:18:36,550 --> 00:18:37,930
He missed...

276
00:18:39,220 --> 00:18:40,890
Are you okay?

277
00:18:40,890 --> 00:18:43,930
He takes right after his father.

278
00:18:43,930 --> 00:18:46,270
Isn't he, Captain Ozora?

279
00:18:52,690 --> 00:18:58,200
Natsuko: Tsubasa ran off!

280
00:18:54,570 --> 00:19:02,160
Just as I thought, my little footballer has slacked off again.

281
00:19:02,160 --> 00:19:05,040
Though that's a very Tsubasa-like thing to do.

282
00:19:05,040 --> 00:19:05,700
Captain!

283
00:19:07,210 --> 00:19:09,040
So you were here.

284
00:19:09,540 --> 00:19:11,420
We're approaching Japan.

285
00:19:11,420 --> 00:19:14,840
Yes, I can finally go home.

286
00:19:14,840 --> 00:19:18,260
By the way, how old is your son now?

287
00:19:18,260 --> 00:19:21,390
He turned 10 this year and is in the final year of elementary school.

288
00:19:21,390 --> 00:19:23,300
He's already 10?

289
00:19:23,300 --> 00:19:28,060
So are you getting him a game as a trip gift this time?

290
00:19:28,060 --> 00:19:30,940
No, he's already got his gift.

291
00:19:33,110 --> 00:19:36,030
Besides, it's the most wonderful thing you could imagine.

292
00:19:46,140 --> 00:19:46,840
Here...

293
00:19:55,590 --> 00:19:58,800
Ugh... The ground and sky are spinning.

294
00:19:59,720 --> 00:20:01,590
I'm dizzy...

295
00:20:01,590 --> 00:20:03,430
Hey Tsubasa.

296
00:20:03,430 --> 00:20:07,430
Even for you, this is way too fast.

297
00:20:07,430 --> 00:20:08,930
No, it's not!

298
00:20:13,350 --> 00:20:15,860
But it's going to get dark soon.

299
00:20:15,860 --> 00:20:18,030
It's about time to head home.

300
00:20:18,030 --> 00:20:19,860
Besides, I'm starving.

301
00:20:20,700 --> 00:20:21,860
Not yet!

302
00:20:28,370 --> 00:20:30,750
Roberto said he had high expectations.

303
00:20:34,170 --> 00:20:36,040
We have no choice but to do this.

304
00:20:42,470 --> 00:20:46,140
Even though he can't pull off the overhead kick yet...

305
00:20:46,140 --> 00:20:50,230
...he's able to hit the post every time he tries.

306
00:20:50,850 --> 00:20:52,890
He has amazing control.

307
00:20:53,940 --> 00:20:56,690
# Ozora Tsubasa requests a match #

308
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:05,030
Take a good look.

309
00:21:06,780 --> 00:21:09,410
Yes, at that goal!

310
00:21:11,160 --> 00:21:14,420
That's our target!

311
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:16,630
This time we'll score!

312
00:21:18,090 --> 00:21:19,590
Let's go!

313
00:21:34,190 --> 00:21:36,350
Go in!

314
00:21:39,610 --> 00:21:41,440
It went in!

315
00:21:43,190 --> 00:21:44,820
Incredible!

316
00:21:46,110 --> 00:21:47,200
I did it.

317
00:21:49,910 --> 00:21:51,700
I did it!

318
00:21:52,160 --> 00:21:54,040
You did it, Tsubasa!

319
00:21:54,040 --> 00:21:56,460
You finally pulled off the overhead kick!

320
00:21:56,460 --> 00:21:57,290
Yes!

321
00:21:57,460 --> 00:21:59,420
Hooray, Tsubasa!

322
00:22:06,260 --> 00:22:08,720
You're incredible, Tsubasa!

323
00:22:10,680 --> 00:22:13,890
Wonder kid! Genius kid!

324
00:22:15,350 --> 00:22:17,650
Brazilian expression of emotion...